<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani sugar mills' stocks fall sharply.</title>
<headline>Pakistani sugar mills' stocks fall sharply.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-10-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Pakistan Sugar Mills Association said on Sunday the stocks of refined crystal white sugar from the 1995/96 (July-June) production of 2.47 million tonnes fell to 0.1 million tonnes by September 30.</p>
<p>Dealers had lifted 2.36 million tonnes, or 95.81 percent, of the production and the remaining 4.19 percent remained within the mills, the association said.</p>
<p>Sugar mills plan to start sugarcane crushing early next month.</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
